<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>second day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>At Southampton: Lancashire 569-8 declared  (M.Watkinson 135,</p>
<p>I.Austin 69 not out). Hampshire 171-0 (M.Hayden 90 not out,</p>
<p>S.Laney 67 not out).</p>
<p>At Cheltenham: Durham 86 and 3-0. Gloucestershire 471-6</p>
<p>declared (M.Alleyne 169, R.Russell 103 not out).</p>
<p>At Edgbaston (first day): Warwickshire 2-0 v Somerset when</p>
<p>rain stopped play.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Nottinghamshire 342 (M.Dowman 149).</p>
<p>Leicestershire 143-3 (D.Maddy 75 not out).</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Worcestershire 394 (K.Spiring 150). Essex</p>
<p>230-3 (P.Prichard 120, D.Robinson 81 not out).</p>
<p>At Northampton: Surrey 581-7 declared (A.Brown 170 not out).</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 154-1 (A.Fordham 69 not out, R.Warren 56 not</p>
<p>out).</p>
<p>At Chesterfield: Derbyshire 513-6 declared (V.Clarke 76 not</p>
<p>out). Glamorgan 39-1.</p>
<p>At Lord's: Kent 208 and 157 (J.Kallis 5-54). Middlesex 105</p>
<p>(M.McCague 7-50) and 134-5 (M.Ramprakash 69 not out).</p>
